NAME
    randbit - generate cryptographically secure random bits

SYNOPSIS
    randbit [OPTIONS]

DESCRIPTION
    randbit generates cryptographically secure random values using the
    operating system's random number generator.

OPTIONS
    -b, --bool
        Print "true" or "false".

    -c, --coin
        Print "Heads" or "Tails".

    -i, --int
        Print a random unsigned 32-bit integer.

    -l, --label
        Prefix output with a label.

    --version
        Show version information.

    --help
        Show help.

EXIT STATUS
    0  Success.
    1  Too many arguments.
    2  Too few arguments.
    3  Invalid arguments.
    4  Random number generation failed.

EXAMPLES
    randbit

    randbit --coin

    randbit --int

FILES
    None.

